  "term": "stereocilia",
  "definition": "Stereocilia are delicate structures on mechanosensory hair cells that convert mechanical stimulation into electrical signals. They can be damaged by loud sound or ototoxic drugs, and loss or injury of these structures is linked to hearing damage.",
